    "durationMs": 109457,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n- **`app/Models/Link.php` + migration** — `links` table (`code` unique varchar(20), `url` text, `clicks` counter) persisted in the provided MySQL 8.4 via the `DB_*` env vars, so data and click counts survive restarts (verified: clicks survived a full server restart).\n- **`app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php`** — creates links (generated 6-char codes or validated custom codes, `409` on duplicates), single-link lookup (`404` on unknown), 302 redirect with an exact-once `clicks` increment, and ascending-order listing with `total`. It decodes the JSON body manually so malformed JSON cleanly falls into validation and returns `422 {\"error\": ...}`.\n- **`routes/api.php` + `bootstrap/app.php`** — routes registered with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are `/links`, `/links/{code}`, `/r/{code}` with no `/api` prefix; a custom `ValidationException` renderer guarantees every validation failure returns `422` JSON with an `error` field.\n- **`start.sh`** (executable) — runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `php artisan serve --no-reload --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000` in the foreground, and a **README section** documents the endpoints and startup.\n\nEvery requirement was exercised with curl: 201 creation (auto and custom codes, submitted URL returned unchanged), 409 duplicate, 422 for missing/invalid url, invalid code, and malformed JSON, 404 unknown codes, 302 with exact `Location` header, one increment per redirect hit, correct list ordering, and persistence across restart. Pint passes on all new files, and the server was stopped after testing."
